    "result": "I implemented `add_business_days(start, n, holidays=())` in `solution.py` following `spec.md`. It moves forward or backward by `n` business days (Monday–Friday, excluding holidays), never counts `start` itself, and for `n == 0` returns `start` if it is a business day or the next one otherwise. Inputs are validated as specified: `start` must be a `date` and not a `datetime`, `n` must be an `int` and not a `bool`, and every holiday must be a `date` and not a `datetime`. Holidays are consumed once into a set, so generators work, and weekend holidays have no effect. I wrote `tests/test_solution.py` with 32 cases covering forward and backward moves, weekend starts, the zero case, holidays on and around the start, generator/tuple/set inputs, and the `TypeError` checks. `python -m pytest -q tests` passes with 32 tests. I edited only `solution.py` and `tests/test_solution.py`, and created no other files.",
